{
  "note": [
    "The pin that keeps ONE field-script evaluator honest across two",
    "implementations: engine/afcalc.py + engine/afscript.py (authoritative —",
    "the fill writes what it computes) and renderer/lib/af-calc.ts +",
    "af-script.ts (the live-preview twin, which never writes bytes). Read by",
    "tests/test_afcalc.py and tests/af-corpus.test.ts, which must agree case",
    "for case.",
    "",
    "Every expectation here was computed by the evaluator and then checked",
    "against the reference implementation extracted from the AcroForm",
    "scripting host that ships, unused, inside the pdf.js dependency — so a",
    "row records what the reference does, not what a transcription of it",
    "recalled. Rows that look wrong are the reference being reproduced:",
    "\"1,234\" parses as 1.234, a non-finite value formats empty, a",
    "calculation over no values is 0, and month names are English whatever",
    "the reader's language.",
    "",
    "`js` is a raw /JS body. `script` is the recognized structure, or null",
    "when the body is not one this app runs — that field keeps its bytes and",
    "is reported by name while the rest of the form still calculates."
  ],
